\description{
A family of SuperLearner-compatible learner functions designed for the
iTMLE targeting step. They differ from standard wrappers in one critical
way: the logit offset is passed as a \strong{column} in \code{X} (named
\code{._sl_offset}) rather than via the \code{offset} argument. This is necessary
because SuperLearner's internal cross-validation subsetting drops the
\code{offset} vector, whereas a column in \code{X} is correctly subset.

Each learner:
\enumerate{
\item Extracts \code{._sl_offset} from \code{X}/\code{newX} via \code{extract_offset()}.
\item Fits a fluctuation model with that offset.
\item Returns predictions on the probability scale, clipped to \verb{[bounds, 1-bounds]}.
}

Learners available:
\describe{
\item{\code{SL.tgt.empty}}{No fluctuation: returns \code{expit(offset)} unchanged.
Acts as the "no update" option.}
\item{\code{SL.tgt.intercept}}{One-parameter intercept fluctuation (standard
TMLE update).}
\item{\code{SL.tgt.glm}}{Main-terms logistic GLM fluctuation with offset.}
\item{\code{SL.tgt.glmnet}}{Penalised logistic regression (elastic net) with
offset via \code{glmnet::cv.glmnet()}.}
\item{\code{SL.tgt.xgboost}}{Gradient boosted trees with offset via
\code{base_margin}. CUDA-capable.}
}

Pre-configured variants (\verb{SL.tmle_*}) expose specific hyperparameter
choices and are the recommended building blocks for \code{sl_tmle}:
\describe{
\item{\code{SL.tmle_empty}}{No fluctuation (pass-through).}
\item{\code{SL.tmle_intercept}}{One-parameter intercept (standard TMLE update).}
\item{\code{SL.tmle_glm}}{Main-terms logistic GLM.}
\item{\code{SL.tmle_glmnet_ridge}}{Ridge regression (alpha = 0).}
\item{\code{SL.tmle_glmnet_enet}}{Elastic net (alpha = 0.5).}
\item{\code{SL.tmle_glmnet_lasso}}{Lasso (alpha = 1).}
\item{\code{SL.tmle_xgb_d1}}{XGBoost depth 1, CPU, 50 rounds.}
\item{\code{SL.tmle_xgb_d3}}{XGBoost depth 3, CPU, 50 rounds.}
\item{\code{SL.tmle_xgb_d6}}{XGBoost depth 6, CPU, 50 rounds.}
}

The default \code{sl_tmle} vector follows Luedtke et al. (2017) Algorithm 4:
